epository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6129882868","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/67#issuecomment-6129882868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/67","id":6129882868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABbV6W9A","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T18:08:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T18:08:20Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** C\n**Automated operational score:** 70/100 — MEDIUM — APPROVE_WITH_COMMENTS\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **HIGH · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Custom role grants wildcard subscription-scoped actions far exceeding documented task requirements**\n  - Category rationale: The Terraform code in tc11_iam.tf grants `actions = [\"*\"]` at subscription scope, which is a wildcard owner-equivalent permission. The tc11_requirements.tf file in the same PR explicitly states that only two read-scoped actions are required for the documented task. The gap between the configured permission set and the documented minimum is directly evidenced in the supplied files, constituting a concrete least-privilege violation and potential privilege-escalation path.\n  - Evidence: In `terraform/tc11_iam.tf`: `resource \"azurerm_role_definition\" \"tc11_reporting_role\"` sets `permissions { actions = [\"*\"] not_actions = [] }` and `assignable_scopes = [data.azurerm_subscription.tc11_current.id]`. In `terraform/tc11_requirements.tf`: `tc11_required_actions` documents only `[\"Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups/read\", \"Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resources/read\"]`. The role description itself states \"permissions exceed the documented reporting task.\" Checkov CKV_AZURE_39 independently flagged this resource.\n  - Analysis: The role `PROM06-TC11-Reporting-Role` in `azurerm_role_definition.tc11_reporting_role` sets `actions = [\"*\"]` with an empty `not_actions` list, assigning every Azure control-plane action to any principal assigned this role at the full subscription scope (`data.azurerm_subscription.tc11_current.id`). The co-located `tc11_requirements.tf` ground-truth file documents that the role exists only to support a read-only reporting task requiring exactly `Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups/read` and `Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resources/read`. A wildcard `actions` at subscription scope is functionally equivalent to the built-in Owner role, enabling any assigned principal to create, modify, or delete any resource, assign other roles (including to themselves or external identities), and exfiltrate data across the entire subscription. Even as a research test fixture, deploying this role to a real subscription creates a standing privilege-escalation surface if any principal is assigned to it or if the subscription ID is reused.\n  - Impact: Any principal assigned this role gains subscription-owner-equivalent control-plane access: resource creation/deletion, role assignments (enabling further privilege escalation to other identities), and access to all data planes reachable from subscription-level management. Even without an explicit assignment in this PR, the role is assignable at subscription scope once deployed and represents a persistent high-privilege standing capability.\n  - Recommendation: Replace `actions = [\"*\"]` with the minimum set documented in `tc11_requirements.tf`: `[\"Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups/read\", \"Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resources/read\"]`. Remove or narrow `assignable_scopes` to the smallest applicable scope (e.g., the research resource group rather than the full subscription). If the wildcard permission is intentional as a deliberate misconfiguration for detection testing, add explicit pipeline controls (e.g., a Sentinel/policy deny or deployment gate) to prevent the role from being assigned to any principal, and document this intent in the PR body and a corresponding test plan rather than only in a source comment.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6129882868/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"GitHub Actions","description":"Automate your workflow from idea to production","external_url":"https://help.github.com/en/actions","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","created_at":"2018-07-30T09:30:17Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T16:17:48Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","artifact_metadata":"write","attestations":"write","checks":"write","code_quality":"write","contents":"write","copilot_requests":"write","deployments":"write","discussions":"write","drives":"write","issues":"write","merge_queues":"write","metadata":"read","models":"read","packages":"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repos